nd also at a point  where his door is taken away from him at  the end of the season he's meant to be  flying out to la in order to meet with  her but instead he ends up heading back  to seemingly stop the games all of these  similarities make me think that illness  wasn't just playing the games in order  to see what they were like but he was  also trying to find a replacement  illness has no heirs or people to pass  his legacy to and thus i believe that he  went through the selection process in  order to see if there was anyone else  worthy to take up the leadership of the  games now this definitely has been seen  in the past and how they've operated in  episode 5 we learned that in ho aka the  front man had actually been a part of  the games and because he's still alive  it's likely that he won them he's also  been drafted into the running of the  games probably because he's now so rich  that he realizes he has more in common  with illness and the like than he does  the typical man that being said i have  no idea how much that amount of money  actually is worth and maybe he still  needs a job anyway this idea of gyun  becoming closer to those in power is  pretty much telegraphed to us at the end  not only does he completely change his  appearance and start dressing smarter  but he also dyes his hair red red  throughout the series is seen as a color  that showcases power and whether it was  the chords given out by the recruiters  or the gods themselves red indicates  someone is part of the system rather  than being a player thus i think the  reason that ilnam created the games is  because he not only wanted a fun time  for him and his friends but he also  wanted someone to take over them in the  finale we learned that the games are  still going on and thus they are likely  looking for other people to either watch  over it or to run it illness has left a  void in the operation that needs to be  filled and i'd absolutely love to see  guillain step into it gina's  demo