ophile so i didn't mind it that much  but yeah it did feel like it was lacking  slightly i'd say it's pretty much equal  to what you get out most flat screens  these days so you'll know from that  whether you want additional speakers or  not now whilst the dongle is also a nice  addition it's also missing some apps at  the moment but if you've got a fire  stick or something to that effect you  shouldn't really notice too much as you  can of course use that instead overall  though i really really love the  projector and if you're looking to move  in this direction i definitely think  it's the way to go so for the picture  i'm gonna score a 10 out of 10 and  that's purely because i haven't really  seen an image better it's cinema quality  and it perfectly projects 4k uhd discs  and it also streams in really high  quality for sound i'm going to give it a  6 out of 10 and that's just due to the  limitations of the speaker on board it  you probably will want to buy additional  ones if you want the full cinematic  experience at home but it's nothing too  bad now for usability i'm going to give  it a 9 out of 10 and that's because of  the remote  overall though really good projector and  thank you to benq for setting it up for  me to review now finally we're going to  be talking about whether jun ho is still  alive at the end of squid game  throughout the series we watched as he  investigate his brother's whereabouts  and he was shot by him at the end his  body was never found and there are some  hints that he's still alive and that he  managed to escape now the first tease is  that he got shot in a similar position  to his brother the pair both fire at one  another and it's an almost eye for a  nice situation we know that in-house  survives the bullet wound and therefore  it is possible that jungle does too  there is definitely a lot of options for  him to take to get out of there and  personally i believe that he made it now  one of the counter-arguments to this is  that